        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="385" ezremote:identifier="title" name="Title" type="ezstring">
          <text>Front-end editing with expwt</text>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="386" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
              <embed size="original" view="embed" align="center" object_remote_id="ezdemo-img-blog-expwt"/>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>Editors spend most of their day on the site, not in the administration interface. expwt puts the most common actions on the page itself: edit, create, move, hide and translate.</paragraph>
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>How it works</header>
                <paragraph>When an editor is signed in, expwt adds a slim toolbar that knows the page you are on. It only shows what your role allows, and every change goes through the same drafts, versions and workflows as in the administration interface.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>For developers</header>
                <paragraph>Designs include one template to show the toolbar. Its scripts load through the system's script packer and run under a strict Content Security Policy.</paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
